%I A163566 #15 Oct 29 2026 00:03:51
%S A163566 10,972,85022,8077072,873994338,109051496360
%N A163566 Total number of grid diagrams of nontrivial knots on grid size n.
%C A163566 From page 3 of Baldridge/McCarthy reference.
%C A163566 Note that creating grid diagrams with sizes above 8 is time intensive and the computation to rule out unknot grid diagrams grows quickly beyond the capabilities of most computers. Baldridge and McCarty highlight some of the differences between cube diagrams and grid diagrams, list examples of small cube diagrams for all knots up to 7 crossings, and give some examples of links.
%H A163566 Scott Baldridge and Ben McCarty, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/0907.5401">Small examples of cube diagrams of knots</a>, arXiv:0907.5401 [math.GT], 2009.
%H A163566 Werner Alois Stanggassinger, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23660288">Grid diagrams of nontrivial knots: a(9) and a(10) of OEIS A163566</a>, Zenodo, 2026.
